-- title:
--   The shared stage of Theorem 30 with batched band arrays, in every program beginning with base58B
-- statement:
--   For every $R$ and standard limits, the program `base58B ++ R` meets `SharedSpecB lim (base58B ++ R) cShared30`: the shared stage (procedure `pSharedP`) of the data structure of Theorem 30 with pruned encodings, run on a source $X\in\mathbb Z^{K_0N\times D}$ at `aX` and the transpose of $Y\in\mathbb Z^{D\times K_0N}$ at `aY`, returns within `cShared30 * sharedShapeP p` steps and leaves the shared data (tables, encodings of every band of the batched input arrays `bArrayL`, `bArrayR`) in place (`SharedReadyA`).
--
--   `base58B` is `base58P` (the 58 procedures of Theorem 30 with pruned encodings) with the body `bandArrayBBody` at the number of bandArray.
--
--   The batched layout (`Batch/Tiling`): the source of the left side is a $K_0N\times D$ matrix $X$ (row by row), that of the right side a $D\times K_0N$ matrix $Y$ (stored transposed); the slot $(g,h)$ of the band $\beta$ holds the row block number $(\beta K_0+g)K_0+h$ of the source, so one run of Theorem 30's data structure computes $K_0^2$ independent block products.
